  "question": "What does the chart suggest about the diversification and changing importance of different export destinations?",
  "status": "complete",
  "createdAt": "2026-09-21T17:08:11.406916Z",
  "completedAt": "2026-09-21T17:08:50.678176Z",
  "answers": {
    "vision": {
      "answer": "U.S. agricultural exports became more diversified between 1995–99 and 2011–15. High-income Asia-Pacific and Europe/Central Asia lost substantial share, while developing East Asia rose sharply from 8% to 23% and North America increased from 22% to 28%; other regions remained relatively small or changed only modestly.",
